<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pact of Biak-na-Bato</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution">Philippine Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pact of Biak-na-Bato was a truce agreed in December 1897 between the Spanish governor-general Fernando Primo de Rivera and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a>'s revolutionaries, mediated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-paterno">Pedro Paterno</a>. Aguinaldo and other leaders accepted exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> in return for payments and promised reforms. Neither side fully honoured it, and the revolution resumed in 1898 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish-American War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pact-of-biak-na-bato.jpg" alt="Pact of Biak-na-Bato" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Hongkong_Junta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
